{"id": "WR16U-9", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Not in the model: a review moderation queue and a separate low-stock transfer object.** The round prompt names the review moderation queue as an example of an admin screen. Reviews are written and shown on the product only. The admin screens converted are the dashboard (KPI tiles), the order work queue (\"Orders (30 days)\", \"All orders\"), the return-request queue and the quotes. Low stock shares the `ProductInfo` table with the product CRUD, so its card layout would change both; it is a tile of the dashboard. "}
{"id": "WR16U-10", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Older specs expected markup that earlier rounds had already changed.** The drawer spec expected the side drawer of round 8 (the top bar of round 15 has Products and Cart and drop-downs), the menu-order test expected a flat menu, the F51 branding test clicked group entries as top-level buttons, F40's Hungarian label for the cart needed a non-exact name (the nav items carry a dot icon). Updated, not worked around: `drawer.spec.ts`, `level4.spec.ts` (menu order), `level5.spec.ts`, `level6b.spec.ts`. The shared selectors for rows that are cards or table rows (`cell`, `dataRows`, `emptyList`, `seekCell`, `sortOrdered`) are in `tests/helpers-customer.ts`. "}
{"id": "WR16U-11", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**A full build is still needed for every frontend change that the Playwright suites see.** `./judo.sh build -f -i` regenerates the frontend files but the served application (Karaf) only changes after the full `./judo.sh build -i` and a restart (about 9 minutes with the restart); frontend work was done against the Vite dev server (`VITE_API_DEFAULT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8181 npx vite`) with `playwright.dev.config.ts`. Related to R16-5. "}
{"id": "WR16U-12", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Profile addresses stay a generated table.** The profile is an editing form with create/update/delete of addresses in the owner's draft; the cards route (R16U-2) would have to re-implement it. The first conversion dropped \"Create\" there; reverted, `CustomerAccountInfo.addresses` is a table again. The same rows are cards in \"My addresses\". "}
{"id": "WR16U-13", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Company pages take 4-9 s with 148 products (a model/performance problem found by the tests; not caused by the UI work).** `POST /Admin/AdminCompanyInfo/~get` and the company list take 4-9 s; `pg_stat_activity` shows one query that computes the derived product fields (`onSale`, `lowStock`, `priceLabel`, ...) for the company-price rows' products, and it grows with the number of products and companies (118 companies, 148 products, 380 orders). Order, product and category lists answer in 0.03-0.5 s. The level 7 specs therefore wait up to 45 s for a response (`slowOpen`, `expect` timeout 15 s in `playwright.local.config.ts`). Suggested for a later round: map the company price's product with only the fields the page shows (a smaller transfer object), or index the join. "}
{"id": "WR16U-14", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Specs and stock: seeded products are bought by the tests and never restocked.** After a few runs \"Wool socks\", \"Day pack\" and others were sold out and unrelated tests failed. `ensureStock(...)` in `tests/helpers-customer.ts` (called in `beforeAll` of the specs that buy seeded products) raises the stock through the admin UI when it is low. The root cause (tests share one database and never clean up) is R16-15 / R16U-8. "}
{"id": "WR16U-15", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**A cards list shows no table operations unless the hook adds them (found by four specs).** Besides R16U-4: row operations of the table (approve and reject of a return request, \"Request return\", remove of a member) are in the container's `actions` and a card must render them itself; the row operation menus of the tables (three dots) have no counterpart. The shared `makeRowCard` renders `rowActions`, delete and remove; the relation lists pass the page's `<relation>OpenPageAction`, `RowDeleteAction`, `RemoveAction` through `TableProxyProps.actions`. "}
{"id": "WR16U-16", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**The group titles of the top bar are not translated.** \"My account\", \"Company\", \"Sell\" stay English in the Hungarian UI (the entries inside are translated). They are plain strings in `registerShellHooks.ts` (round 15); the menu items customizer has no i18n hook. Noted, not fixed. "}
{"id": "WR16U-17", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Admin specs and the shared data, and what the reservation job does to exact counts.** The admin Playwright project failed 17 of 35 tests because its specs looked for the 8 seeded products on one page of a table with some 250 products; the seed created a category and a product a second time when the row was on page 2 (\"Identifier attribute is not unique\", two \"Footwear\" categories; the duplicate was removed with one SQL delete, it was created by the first run of this round and had no products). Fixed in the specs, not in the data: `seek` pages to the row, the seed checks with `seek`, typing into the generated dialogs is verified and retried (the first field has the focus and takes the first keys; \"Commission (%)\" of the category dialog is required). Separately, the unpaid orders of earlier tests are cancelled by the reservation job (F73) at any time, which changes the counts of the day (F48) and the stock of seeded products (F23, F49) between two readings; those specs now check the direction of the change, not an exact number. Product price, stock and the name of a seeded product are changed by the shop tests and not restored (`ensureStock` only raises stock). "}
{"id": "WR16U-18", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Flaky under load: F49 (level6b:85) and F48 (level6b:208), and the Keycloak login timeouts of pw-r16u-q (no product defect).** pw-r16u-final passed 78/78, pw-r16u-final2 76/2. Rerun once each, serially, `--retries=0`: both pass (F49 1.7 min, F48 51 s). Causes: F49 failed on a 10 s `locator.click` timeout (slow page while the Docker VM was loaded; the same spec passes alone); F48 compared the day's order count with a reading taken earlier (expected 97, received 0), which the reservation job (F73) and the data shared with earlier specs can change at any time (see R16U-17). pw-r16u-q had 14 of 15 failures waiting 40 s for `#kc-form-login`; Keycloak (`keycloak-webshop`, port 8280, `/auth`) had 0 restarts, no OOM and answered in 2-10 ms afterwards, other stacks on the same Docker VM were competing for it; the 15 specs pass when re-run (17 passed, 15.3 min). Run Playwright with `-c playwright.local.config.ts --workers=1` and keep other Docker stacks idle during full runs. "}
{"id": "WR16U-19", "src": "webshop-R16U", "target": "", "text": "**Flaky: F23 (level3-customer:175), final6 failed once (expected stock 57, received 58).** Rerun alone, `--retries=0`: passes (1.8 min). Cause: shared data. The reservation job (F73) cancels old unpaid orders at any time and gives their stock back between two readings, so an exact stock number moves by one. The spec was already changed to check the direction of the change in other places (R16U-17); this one assertion stays exact. Not a product defect. ## Round 17 (Level 9b: F76-F79) "}
{"id": "WR17-1", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**`kb_get` of a blueprint or best practice returns only the intro line (again, R16U-1).** `kb_get(path)` of `best-practices/backend/scheduled-data-sync-pipeline.md`, `best-practices/model/external-system-staging-entity.md` answered with the Intent paragraph and \"(+7 more sections in this file)\"; the `kb_search` hits of these files carry only the title as `headingPath` (chunk `:meta`), so no `section` can be copied. The files were read from disk (`/Users/bmiller/Projects/judo-blueprint/catalog/...`). With a `headingPath` from `kb_search` (agent-docs files) `kb_get(path, section)` worked (schema-evolution, build-process, architectural-patterns). There are no `.agent.md` companions for blueprints or best practices, only for agent-docs. "}
{"id": "WR17-2", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**JUDO CLI: how to create a MIME type, and a binary type with two MIME types.** `judo-cli.agent.md` says `create -t MimeType -n ...` fails (no name) but gives no working form. Found with `create --schema -t MimeType` (route `addMimeType(model, type, subType)`): `create -t MimeType --ns webshop -s type=application -s subType=json`. `BinaryType.mimeTypes` takes ONE value on `create` (`-s mimeTypes=a,b` is rejected) and `--add mimeTypes=...` is rejected too; both print `valid hu.blackbelt...MimeTypeImpl@2f27c354 \u00b7 ...` (the valid values as object hashes, unreadable) and exit 0, so a script goes on. The failed `create -t BinaryType` left the input member without a data type, and the validation then said \"ImportRunInfo_Table::startImport::FormCall have to be presented in container\": a misleading message for a missing type (found by `--schema`/`status`). Route: two file members on the input (`csvFile` with the CSV type, `jsonFile` with a JSON type) and a check in the operation that exactly one is given. "}
{"id": "WR17-3", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**Mail: `JUDO_PLATFORM_MAIL_SMTP_HOST/PORT` in `judo-karaf.env` is not enough to get an `EmailService` (deployment doc incomplete).** `agent-docs/deployment/application-config.md` \"6. Email (SMTP)\" says: for Mailpit point host and port at `localhost:1025` in `judo-karaf.env`. With host, port, `_AUTH=false` and `JUDO_PLATFORM_LOG_SMTP_SERVER=false` the application started, but the `EmailService` OSGi service did not exist (my `@Reference` was null: \"The platform mail service is not available\"): `JavaMailSenderActivator` has `configuration-policy=require` and its configuration is created from `judo-platform-config-templates/hu.blackbelt.email.impl.JavaMailSenderActivator.xml`, whose condition is `logSmtpServer || (mailSmtpUser && mailSmtpPassword && mailSmtpHost all set)`. With the log server off, user and password must be set too (any value; `AUTH=false` keeps them unused). Final `judo-karaf.env`: HOST=localhost, PORT=1025, USER=mailpit, PASSWORD=mailpit, AUTH=false, STARTTLS_ENABLE=false, FROM, `LOG_SMTP_SERVER=false`. Read from the jar in `.karaf/system/hu/blackbelt/judo/platform/judo-platform-config-templates`. "}
{"id": "WR17-4", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**Mail doc: port of the log SMTP server.** The same section says the log SMTP server listens on `logSmtpServerPort`, \"which defaults to `1025`\"; the shipped template `hu.blackbelt.email.impl.LogSmtpServer.template` says `${logSmtpServerPort ! \"10025\"}` (and the component XML property is 10025). Read, not run (the log server was off). "}
{"id": "WR17-5", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**`handlebars-email-template.md` renders twice if the example is copied.** The example compiles the template itself and hands the result to the mail builder as `htmlTemplate`; `platform-behavior-reference.agent.md` \"Email Service\" says `htmlTemplate`/`plaintTemplate` ARE Handlebars templates applied to `model`, and `subject` is NOT a template. The result of the first rendering is rendered a second time (a value that contains `{{` would be eaten). Used here: the shop renders subject and body itself (to keep the text in the outbox and in the \"Sent mails\" screen) and passes the text with an empty model. The best practice does not say which of the two is the intended split. "}
{"id": "WR17-6", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**An unsent optional member of an operation input is `null`, not `Optional.empty()`.** `BulkImportInput.getJsonFile()` (an optional transient binary) threw a NullPointerException on `.isPresent()` when the client sent only the CSV file; `JobInput.getAsOf()` behaves the same (the F73 code of R16 already checked `== null`). Neither the agent-docs (\"Optional types: true\" in the generated DAO headers) nor `custom-operations.md` mention it. The implementations check `x != null && x.isPresent()`. "}
{"id": "WR17-7", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**`build -a` is documented as \"fast Java iteration\", but `start` runs the previous code.** `build-process.agent.md` \"`judo.sh build` flag reference\": \"`-a` builds `app/` module only (fast Java iteration)\". After `./judo.sh build -a -i -M -F` the running application was stopped, and `./judo.sh start` unpacks the `karaf-offline` tarball, which still held the old app jar (the new jar was only in `~/.m2`): the tests ran against old code (the mail retry change was not visible). What refreshes the application is `./judo.sh build -i -M -F` (backend + Karaf package, 37 s) then `start` (about 3 minutes until the API answers). Not in the doc. "}
{"id": "WR17-8", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**Dependency coordinates of the platform mail API (catalog: \"check the artifact in your application\").** `email-service-integration.md` and `platform-email-template-service` say the `EmailService` API is not described and to check the dependency. The artifact is `hu.blackbelt:osgi-email-api` (version of `.karaf/system/hu/blackbelt/osgi-email-api/`), compile-only (`provided`) in `generator-overrides/app/pom.xml.extra-dependencies.fragment.hbs`, as Handlebars and the file store in R16U; the integration-test module needs it as a normal dependency (provided scope is not transitive). A catalog line with the coordinates and `scope=provided` would save the search. "}
{"id": "WR17-9", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**Existing singleton row and new attributes with defaults.** After the additive migration the `ShopConfig` row has `carrierDeliveryHours` and `cartReminderHours` = 24 but `mailFrom` empty (and `reservationMinutes` of R16 is empty too): the column default of the migration is not the model default for every attribute. The code treats an empty value as the default (`shop@webshop.local`, 15 minutes). `schema-evolution.agent.md` says an additive change needs no manual step; it does not say that existing rows may get empty values. "}
{"id": "WR17-10", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**Cart \"touched\" is only add-to-cart and checkout.** The generated cart table edits (quantity, remove a line) are built-in operations of the cart line; the interceptor route (agent-docs/backend/interceptors.md) would touch the cart there, but it was not built this round: a customer who only edits the quantity does not start a new quiet period. Own limit, not a catalog gap; listed under \"not done\". "}
{"id": "WR17-11", "src": "webshop-R17", "target": "", "text": "**Flaky / environment.** The import of 5 000 rows takes about 2.5 minutes with 250 rows per transaction (two DAO writes per product: create and link to the run); undo (one transaction, 4 990 deletes) about 40 seconds. The screens stay usable (the spec opens another menu while the batches run and allows 10 seconds for it; it passed). The `Import runs` card list does not refresh by itself: the \"Refresh\" button or reopening the screen shows the progress (the test reopens it). ## Round 18 (Level 10a: F80-F85) "}
